#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:16
msgid "Video 14: I2C 16x2 LCD Display 丨 DHT11 - Humidity and Temperature Sensor 丨 Heat Index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:18
msgid "This tutorial dives into the essentials of connecting and using a DHT11 humidity and temperature sensor and a 16x2 I2C LCD display in Arduino programming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:20
msgid "**DHT11 Sensor**: Explains how to connect and read temperature, humidity, and heat index values from a DHT11 sensor. It covers the importance of using a pull-up resistor and the capability of the sensor to use either 3.3V or 5V power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:21
msgid "**I2C LCD Display**: Guides through connecting and initializing a 16x2 I2C LCD display with the Arduino, highlighting how to save IO pins by using I2C communication. It includes details on adjusting the contrast and backlight of the display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:22
msgid "**Library Installation**: Demonstrates how to install the necessary libraries for DHT11 and I2C LCD display from the Arduino Library Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:23
msgid "**Coding for DHT11 and I2C LCD**: Provides a step-by-step guide on writing code to read data from the DHT11 sensor and display it on the I2C LCD. It includes checking for valid sensor readings and handling errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:24
msgid "**Displaying Data**: Shows how to display temperature, humidity, and heat index on the LCD, including how to alternate between different displays using a delay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_video_course/video_14_I2C 16x2_LCD.rst:25
msgid "**Challenge Activity**: Encourages further learning by adding a button to switch between displaying temperature and heat index in Celsius and Fahrenheit, implementing either millis() function or hardware interrupts for improved functionality."
msgstr ""

